\subsection{Comparative evaluation}
\label{sec:observer-comparison}

\subsubsection{Deterministic external and predecessor baselines}
The deterministic comparison includes adaptive PII, OU--II, and an adapted
vertical-reference configuration of the time-varying-gain nonlinear observer
(TVG--NLO) of Bryne, Fossen, and Johansen~\cite{BryneFossenJohansen2014_TVG_NLO}.
The adapted TVG--NLO omits the horizontal GNSS and compass aiding of the
published full observer, so horizontal position and yaw are unscored.  PII
provides a feedback-based heave reference; OU--II is the immediate stochastic
predecessor of OU--III.

All methods replay the same timestamped synthetic motion and inertial records
and use the final \SI{900}{s}.  The common comparison is vertical displacement
and tilt, available from every method.  Parameters are frozen before evaluation
and reference displacement is never used to select gains.  OU--II and OU--III
share the same wave-band period input; OU--III uses the deployed integral-state
schedule of Sec.~\ref{sec:adaptation}, including cadence renormalization,
whereas OU--II uses its second-order position/velocity regularizers.

