In this single-realization comparison, OU--III has the lowest mean normalized
vertical-displacement RMS error: \pct{\OUBaselineOUIIIMeanVerticalPercent} of
$H_s$, versus \pct{\OUBaselineOUIIMeanVerticalPercent} for OU--II,
\pct{\OUBaselinePIIMeanVerticalPercent} for PII, and
\pct{\OUBaselineTVGNLOMeanVerticalPercent} for adapted TVG--NLO.  These values
are reproducible external references, not ensemble estimates; inferential
OU-family claims use the paired study below.

Only OU--II is evaluated under the full paired protocol, so the strongest
statistical comparison is with the predecessor rather than a ranking against
published practice.  Adapted TVG--NLO also differs from its GNSS/compass-aided
published experiment, and no conventional frequency-domain double-integration
baseline is included.

